CODEGEN.md §2.4 (DECISIONS 342, settled 2026-10-09): an output inside the project is judged from the project directory, even when its root lies inside the project: a committed link there, as the root's own directory `res`, is E8027 naming it.
-- project.canon --
project acme {
  canon: "0.1"
  roots {
    res: "res"
  }
}
-- a/a.canon --
/// A.
package a

/// Note.
@text("note.txt")
export fn note() -> String { return "n\n" }

emit text { out: "@res/notes" }
-- ../Resource/notes/keep.txt --
keep
-- links --
res ../Resource
-- findings.txt --
error[E8027]  a/a.canon:8:18
  refusing to write @res/notes/note.txt: @res is a symbolic link, and a build never writes through one

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
